# The Debian packages the chorus-soloist image carries (tools/soloist-image.sh stages exactly
# these, each verified against its sha256; tools/conventions/check-pins.sh holds this file's
# shape; the decision record "the chorus-soloist image" in docs/decisions says why this method).
#
# What it is: the Depends closure (no Recommends) of pipewire, pipewire-bin and wireplumber
# over the package set of the base image debian:trixie-20260918-slim, resolved on 2026-10-03
# against snapshot.debian.org at the timestamp below (the timestamp the base image itself was
# built from), less the twelve packages listed under "excluded". PipeWire 1.4.2 and
# WirePlumber 0.5.8 are what goal 17's probe measured.
#
# How it was resolved (apt with private state, no root; <base> is the base image unpacked):
#   apt-get -o Dir::Etc::sourcelist=<a file naming the three suites below at the snapshot>
#     -o Dir::State::status=<base>/var/lib/dpkg/status -o Dir::State::lists=<dir>
#     -o Dir::Cache::archives=<dir> -o Debug::NoLocking=1 update
#   apt-get <the same options> install --print-uris --no-install-recommends
#     pipewire pipewire-bin wireplumber
#   suites: debian trixie main, debian trixie-updates main, debian-security trixie-security main
# It named 72 packages, all from the debian archive. A package's source name and version are
# its control file's Source field (a +bN rebuild suffix removed). Moving a pin is its own
# commit: resolve again at a newer timestamp with the base image of that date.
#
# snapshot = 20260918T000000Z
# archive = https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/
#
# excluded: systemd systemd-sysv libsystemd-shared libpam-systemd libapparmor1
# excluded: dbus dbus-bin dbus-daemon dbus-session-bus-common dbus-system-bus-common
# excluded: dbus-user-session adduser
#   (wireplumber Depends on a D-Bus session bus, which Depends on systemd's user session. A
#   receiver runs PipeWire and WirePlumber with D-Bus off and no init system, so the bus
#   daemon and systemd are never started; libdbus-1-3, the library the modules link, stays.
#   The image test proves no staged program or library needs a file of an excluded package.)
#
# Columns: package version architecture sha256 size source-package source-version path
